    app -> css "m4 · GET resource (agent, client, issuer, didvc)" {
      technology "HTTPS"
      notes """
        **Phase 2 — access request** (traces `3323226b…` OPTIONS, `3c58b6bb…` GET).
        `GET /my-pod/test-folder/dual-mode-resource.txt`. In the model m4 = (DID_i, DID_u, DID_a, uri):
        the issuer the user trusts, the user, the app and the resource.

        Request headers:

        ```json
        {
          "agent": "did:web:bboi.solidcommunity.net:public",
          "client": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public",
          "issuer": "did:web:secureissuer.solidcommunity.net:public",
          "didvc": "true"
        }
        ```
        """
    }

    css -> app "VPR · 401 www-authenticate: didcomm proofRequest" {
      technology "HTTPS"
      notes """
        The CSS answers with the **Verifiable Presentation Request** (VPR in the model: attributes, uri,
        `nc`, DID_v). It travels base64-encoded in `www-authenticate: didcomm proofRequest="…"`.
        `options.challenge` is the nonce **n_c** that ends up in Y and in the commitment C;
        `requestACP` binds the request to target, owner, issuer, client and agent.

        Decoded `proofRequest`:

        ```json
        {
          "@context": [
            "https://bboi.solidcommunity.net/public/schemas/202…e.jsonld"
          ],
          "type": [
            "VerifiablePresentationRequest"
          ],
          "presentation_definition": {
            "id": "32f54163-7166-48f1-93d8-ff217bdb0653",
            "input_descriptors": [
              {
                "id": "unisa_student",
                "name": "University of Salerno Demo",
                "purpose": "Demonstrate to be a student from the University of…this POD",
                "constraints": {
                  "fields": [
                    {
                      "path": [
                        "$.credentialSubject.degree",
                        "$.credentialSubject.claims.degree"
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            ],
            "format": {
              "ldp_vc": {
                "proof_type": [
                  "JsonWebSignature2020",
                  "Ed25519Signature2018",
                  "EcdsaSecp256k1Signature2019",
                  "RsaSignature2018"
                ]
              },
              "ldp_vp": {
                "proof_type": [
                  "Ed25519Signature2018"
                ]
              },
              "ldp": {
                "proof_type": [
                  "RsaSignature2018"
                ]
              }
            },
            "requestACP": {
              "type": [
                "ACPContext"
              ],
              "target": "http://localhost:3002/my-pod/test-folder/dual-mode-resource.txt",
              "owner": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:Commun…ver:main",
              "issuer": "did:web:secureissuer.solidcommunity.net:public",
              "client": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public",
              "agent": "did:web:bboi.solidcommunity.net:public"
            }
          },
          "options": {
            "challenge": "DIsAJP6aajfSMyGQCsWPjQ==",
            "domain": "https://bboi.solidcommunity.net/definition/ourProtocol#test"
          }
        }
        ```

        Body: `UnauthorizedHttpError`, status 401.
        """
    }

    app -> user "m5 · present-proof/2.0 request-presentation" {
      technology "DIDComm"
      notes """
        **Phase 3 — proof** (trace `28e7f75c…`, `POST /requestUserCredential` on the app). The app wraps the
        VPR (`vc.wrapPresentationRequest`: VPR plus `termsAndCondition`) and signs the wrapper
        (`vc.signWrappedPresentationRequest`), then forwards it to the wallet as a DIF presentation-exchange
        definition.

        Plaintext (`didcomm.pack` on demo-app-1):

        ```json
        {
          "@type": "https://didcomm.org/present-proof/2.0/request-presentation",
          "will_confirm": true,
          "present_multiple": false,
          "formats": [
            {
