    alt "access decision" {
      when "3a — only acl:Read granted (trusted hospital)" {
        css -> app "200 OK + plaintext resource" {
          technology "HTTPS"
          notes """
            **Third run — demo-app-2 (Public Hospital)**, client `did:web:publichospital.solidcommunity.net:public`
            (traces `c79a3b2a…`, `70fd58cd…`, `7f44656d…`, `170830e9…`, `b31760ef…`, `25118f7e…`).
            m1–m7 are the same as above. The client only holds `acl:Read`, so after the VP checks the CSS
            returns the resource in clear — no K_ttp, no NRO, no receipts (`nro-audit/query` stays empty).

            Response body:

            ```text
            This resource has two access modes depending on who asks: secureapp gets it only
            via non-repudiable read (acl:NRRead), secureapp-2 gets it via plain acl:Read.

            ```
            """
        }
      }
      else "3b — only acl:NRRead granted" {
        opt "K_ttp setup — first NRRead only" {
          css -> ttp "m10 · POST /keyExchange" {
            technology "HTTPS"
            notes """
              Setup of **K_ttp** (m10/m11 in the model), done once per CSS process (`ensureTtpKey`); later
              NRReads reuse the key — in the TTP run (`714252ce…`) this exchange is absent.
              The CSS sends an ephemeral X25519 public key signed with its `did:web` key
              (payload tag `VERA-KEX-CSS`).

              Request body:

              ```json
              {
                "did": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:Commun…ver:main",
                "publicKey": "MKr0NbWEr5KaVR3dsAbaYWn0_79qEU4b97x5pV3VcQA",
                "signature": "0CI3gZY8ETRNEsxNixAUMAVWfS3F5jBvzwRMH17aUDlu59Lisz…QX2GpcCA"
              }
              ```
              """
          }

          ttp -> css "m11 · TTP ephemeral key + signature" {
            technology "HTTPS"
            notes """
              The TTP answers with its own ephemeral key, signed over both public keys (tag `VERA-KEX-TTP`).
              Both sides derive K_ttp = HKDF(X25519(own, peer)); `kid` identifies it and prefixes every Y.

              Response body:

              ```json
              {
                "did": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:DKGNon…p:config",
                "publicKey": "9wFdPEDFqqqyYw2cykevo85oy3P6ZCp02QOj3QPUK0k",
                "signature": "xqh1fr6T2vr_K9XM3hCLbQN36W6bhSF-QIYZaCWS6IVQKy5aQc…EsI-5rBw",
                "kid": "395bb593e938de9c19cf6338473a1b60"
              }
              ```
              """
          }
        }

        css -> app "m12 · 200 encryptedresource (E, Y, h, h_K, NRO)" {
          technology "HTTPS"
          notes """
            m12 = (resenc, k15enc, h, h_K, nro) in the model. The CSS generates a fresh resource key K_R and:

            - **E** = AEAD_K_R(R, salt) — the encrypted resource
            - **Y** = kid . AEAD_K_ttp(K_R, DID_A, n_c, H(E)) — K_R in escrow for the TTP
            - **h** = H(R, salt), **h_K** = H(K_R)
            - **C** = H(DID_V, DID_A, DID_U, URI, n_c, H(E), Y, h, h_K) — the commitment
            - **NRO** = CSS signature on C (`vc.issue`, `NonRepudiableOrigin`, `signedHash` = C)

            `encryptedresource` header:

            ```json
            {
              "E": "nePRmiWKTfn_IoFu4yOHKXRHXvrbXc-DkdHta8kQwS1PX0QtOG…7UhpxmcA",
              "Y": "395bb593e938de9c19cf6338473a1b60.OUfG-f9yfmNiH-_Ep…sfs5KQ0g",
              "h": "28b3b5a9a52827c621f219ffda9239e81fb3736bcbe0fa1ac7c72da0d3e71b86",
              "hK": "71b7d68edda23de16a074a20991d6868d15d2a89120faae7ab468c9d5fe63a93",
              "nro": {
                "@context": [
                  "https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1",
                  "https://secureapp.solidcommunity.net/public/NonRep…t.jsonld"
                ],
                "id": "urn:uuid:fb21d1a8-0a5d-4cc6-9c1e-e1f71795b021",
                "type": [
                  "VerifiableCredential",
                  "NonRepudiableOrigin"
                ],
                "issuer": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:Commun…ver:main",
                "issuanceDate": "2026-11-23T17:59:44.15Z",
                "credentialSubject": {
                  "id": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public",
                  "signedHash": "102908bc6f624e631f460b1356009c65dbc1fb6c805a89c4c53af2b2348dff2a"
                },
                "proof": {
                  "verificationMethod": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:Commun…8Gkpkt3A",
                  "type": "Ed25519Signature2018",
                  "created": "2026-11-23T17:59:44Z",
                  "proofPurpose": "assertionMethod",
                  "jws": "eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsImI2NCI6ZmFsc2UsImNyaXQiOlsiYj…pdOwjICg"
                }
              }
            }
            ```
            """
        }

        alt "release path" {
          when "5a — release via CSS" {
            app -> css "m13 · GET resource (signedresource = NRR)" {
              technology "HTTPS"
              notes """
                **Phase 5a — release via CSS** (trace `4fbb8cd9…`). The app UI calls `POST /completeNonRepudiableRelease`
                with `useTtp: false`. The app verifies the NRO (`vc.verifyCredential`), recomputes C and signs it:
                m13 = sig(C, sk_a), the **NonRepudiationDestination** (`signedHash` = C).

                `signedresource` header — the NRR:

                ```json
                {
                  "@context": [
                    "https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1",
                    "https://privateclinic.solidcommunity.net/public/No…t.jsonld"
                  ],
                  "id": "urn:uuid:4b5dec3b-c8bd-4fff-8aa1-8fd022ad5dee",
                  "type": [
                    "VerifiableCredential",
                    "NonRepudiationDestination"
                  ],
                  "issuer": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public",
                  "issuanceDate": "2026-11-23T17:59:47.87Z",
                  "credentialSubject": {
                    "id": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:Commun…ver:main",
                    "signedHash": "102908bc6f624e631f460b1356009c65dbc1fb6c805a89c4c53af2b2348dff2a"
                  },
                  "proof": {
                    "verificationMethod": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public#z6…sKuUGG6R",
                    "type": "Ed25519Signature2018",
                    "created": "2026-11-23T17:59:47Z",
                    "proofPurpose": "assertionMethod",
                    "jws": "eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsImI2NCI6ZmFsc2UsImNyaXQiOlsiYj…RohIOcDA"
                  }
                }
                ```
                """
            }

            css -> app "m14 · 200 keyfordecrypt (K_R)" {
              technology "HTTPS"
              notes """
                The CSS verifies the NRR against the pending release (same C, signed by DID_A), stores it
                (`css.storeVerifiedJws`) and releases K_R. The app decrypts E locally.

                `keyfordecrypt` header:

                ```json
                "JTBXqKWrXaNN1WNLGm4ZrOXnQolJkcf5m1MzCpOapWU"
                ```

                Stored evidence:

                ```json
                {
                  "id": "057fb08619c62fad50e536315d9dbf0eb4a0a240ddedc6581f372299229da77e",
                  "signedResource": "(the NRR above)",
                  "signedResourceType": "vc",
                  "requestedResource": "http://localhost:3002/my-pod/test-folder/dual-mode-resource.txt",
                  "requesterDid": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public",
                  "messageHash": "102908bc6f624e631f460b1356009c65dbc1fb6c805a89c4c53af2b2348dff2a",
                  "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23T17:59:47.915Z",
                  "signerId": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public#z6…sKuUGG6R"
                }
                ```

                Result returned to the app UI:

                ```json
                {
                  "content": "This resource has two access modes depending on wh…l:Read. ",
                  "releasedBy": "css",
                  "commitment": "102908bc6f624e631f460b1356009c65dbc1fb6c805a89c4c53af2b2348dff2a"
                }
                ```
                """
            }
          }
          else "5b — release via TTP" {
            app -> ttp "m15 · POST /checkResource" {
              technology "HTTPS"
              notes """
                **Phase 5b — release via TTP** (second run, trace `3472aa18…`): `POST /completeNonRepudiableRelease`
                with `useTtp: true`. m15 = (uri, n_c, H(E), Y, h, h_K, NRO, m13): everything the TTP needs
                to recompute C, but not E, which never leaves the app.

                Request body:

                ```json
                {
                  "didU": "did:web:bboi.solidcommunity.net:public",
                  "uri": "http://localhost:3002/my-pod/test-folder/dual-mode-resource.txt",
                  "nc": "S1L5AcZhuDt2Soy834MpZw==",
                  "hE": "40c88e39d3e2b61f6b2f285245985307be957c937e5e0010de484b0b2d1d046b",
                  "Y": "395bb593e938de9c19cf6338473a1b60.myLTd70Npgc3YSsyz…4GIU1kgw",
                  "h": "accb2de97f940031d4e2e028ae111bf609d05d50fe9bd187d6f17a5bf1ad6119",
                  "hK": "2aba4a910da8165454039c57f397a0cb18ec7038909d47b0a854b8cd5f2dc1a6",
                  "nro": {
                    "@context": [
                      "https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1",
                      "https://secureapp.solidcommunity.net/public/NonRep…t.jsonld"
                    ],
                    "id": "urn:uuid:5a07b653-403d-4864-9c08-aeaaef621765",
                    "type": [
                      "VerifiableCredential",
                      "NonRepudiableOrigin"
                    ],
                    "issuer": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:Commun…ver:main",
                    "issuanceDate": "2026-11-23T18:12:09.48Z",
                    "credentialSubject": {
                      "id": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public",
                      "signedHash": "b4bf286d5126c77c0b8ee6350bb78d3b557190f709367e2e1fbbe201f41f0a1e"
                    },
                    "proof": {
                      "verificationMethod": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:Commun…8Gkpkt3A",
                      "type": "Ed25519Signature2018",
                      "created": "2026-11-23T18:12:09Z",
                      "proofPurpose": "assertionMethod",
                      "jws": "eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsImI2NCI6ZmFsc2UsImNyaXQiOlsiYj…N8_0xaAg"
                    }
                  },
                  "nrr": {
                    "@context": [
                      "https://www.w3.org/2018/credentials/v1",
                      "https://privateclinic.solidcommunity.net/public/No…t.jsonld"
                    ],
                    "id": "urn:uuid:8e2eaada-2582-4b29-b155-5c9155a78dc8",
                    "type": [
                      "VerifiableCredential",
                      "NonRepudiationDestination"
                    ],
                    "issuer": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public",
                    "issuanceDate": "2026-11-23T18:12:11.24Z",
                    "credentialSubject": {
                      "id": "did:web:raw.githubusercontent.com:biagioboi:Commun…ver:main",
                      "signedHash": "b4bf286d5126c77c0b8ee6350bb78d3b557190f709367e2e1fbbe201f41f0a1e"
                    },
                    "proof": {
                      "verificationMethod": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public#z6…sKuUGG6R",
                      "type": "Ed25519Signature2018",
                      "created": "2026-11-23T18:12:11Z",
                      "proofPurpose": "assertionMethod",
                      "jws": "eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsImI2NCI6ZmFsc2UsImNyaXQiOlsiYj…KqLOiCCQ"
                    }
                  }
                }
                ```

                The TTP does all the checks (`checkResource`, as in the model):

                1. opens **Y** with K_ttp (selected by `kid`) and checks it is bound to DID_A (the NRR signer), n_c and H(E);
                2. checks H(K_R) = **h_K**;
                3. recomputes **C** and checks the NRO is the CSS signature on C;
                4. checks the NRR (m13) is the app signature on C;
                5. stores the NRR in its own `nrr-audit`.
                """
            }

            ttp -> app "m16 · keyForDecrypt (K_R)" {
              technology "HTTPS"
              notes """
                Only after all checks pass the TTP releases K_R to the app. The release never waits for the CSS,
                which may be offline or a party to the dispute.

                Response body:

                ```json
                {
                  "keyForDecrypt": "VNBo8G_d6otS-Nw8pKXyUX4u0tvYiEzVbSs5-rqm_8I",
                  "commitment": "b4bf286d5126c77c0b8ee6350bb78d3b557190f709367e2e1fbbe201f41f0a1e",
                  "nrrRecordId": "8d03bc9d009de25fe8d542af958f1728ad03cb1bbab2ba5f7a7b795d01cc094b"
                }
                ```

                Result returned to the app UI:

                ```json
                {
                  "content": "This resource has two access modes depending on wh…l:Read. ",
                  "releasedBy": "ttp",
                  "commitment": "b4bf286d5126c77c0b8ee6350bb78d3b557190f709367e2e1fbbe201f41f0a1e"
                }
                ```
                """
            }

            ttp -> css "m17 · forward NRR (ttpreceipt)" {
              technology "HTTPS"
              notes """
                After m16 the TTP forwards the NRR to the CSS, so the origin also gets its proof of receipt.
                No check happens here on the TTP side: it is a delivery, sealed under K_ttp
                (`kid . AEAD_K_ttp({nrr, uri})`, tag `VERA-M17`) so the CSS knows it comes from the TTP it shares
                K_ttp with. It travels as the `ttpreceipt` header of a `GET` on the resource; the CSS answers 200
                with no body.

                `ttpreceipt` header:

                ```json
                "395bb593e938de9c19cf6338473a1b60.deY0EbFsWCAhzgVAk…OaNgbDSg"
                ```

                The CSS (`acceptNrrFromTtp`) opens the receipt, checks the NRR is the app signature on C and stores it:

                Stored evidence:

                ```json
                {
                  "id": "5059f9e02b76f3d30cf7760710c943db49b5af688c46ce7ae437f047ecb1d105",
                  "signedResource": "(the NRR of m15)",
                  "signedResourceType": "vc",
                  "requestedResource": "http://localhost:3002/my-pod/test-folder/dual-mode-resource.txt",
                  "requesterDid": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public",
                  "messageHash": "b4bf286d5126c77c0b8ee6350bb78d3b557190f709367e2e1fbbe201f41f0a1e",
                  "verifiedAt": "2026-11-23T18:12:11.572Z",
                  "signerId": "did:web:privateclinic.solidcommunity.net:public#z6…sKuUGG6R"
                }
                ```
                """
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }

    app -> user "Deliver resource" {
      notes """
        The app shows the decrypted resource — same plaintext on both release paths
        (`releasedBy = css` in 5a, `releasedBy = ttp` in 5b).

        Plaintext:

        ```text
        This resource has two access modes depending on who asks: secureapp gets it only
        via non-repudiable read (acl:NRRead), secureapp-2 gets it via plain acl:Read.

        ```

        Then `GET /.internal/nro-audit/query`: 1 record after the CSS release (`47686a35…`),
        2 after the TTP release (`d505b100…`).
        """
    }
  }

  view context {
    title "Participants overview"
    include *
    include -> css
    include -> app
    include -> ttp
  }
}